 {"id":"CF-248","title":"P2 - cf-node checkout drift (superseded: node sits at origin/main as of 2026-11-05, verify-node.sh exits 3 UNVERIFIED pending CF-224)","status":"pending","priority":"P2","complexity":1,"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-05 by the critical-path audit: the cf-node checkout is 2 commits behind origin/main and scripts/verify-node.sh FAILs when run there. The dispatch leg hands cf-node the repo to run in, so a node two commits stale is a second source of truth: any fix landed on main is absent exactly where the work runs, and a verification script that fails on the node cannot distinguish stale checkout from broken node. Not yet attributed: whether the failure is only the stale commits or also a real node defect, which is why this row is P2 and scoped to making verify-node.sh pass against current origin/main before any conclusion is drawn about the node itself.","acceptance_criteria":"1. scripts/verify-node.sh exits 0 on cf-node against current origin/main. 2. The cf-node checkout reports git rev-list --count HEAD..origin/main as 0 after a fetch, and the row note records both the HEAD it was on and the HEAD it was brought to. 3. If verify-node.sh still fails after the checkout is current, the failure is quoted verbatim in the row note and this row is re-scoped to the real defect rather than closed.","probe":null,"created_at":"2026-11-05T13:03:23Z","updated_at":"2026-11-05T13:04:22Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"0b5f8a286f46bdea1bb4a9a1218c83728f835a7e4df014b0837c7415683efa53"},"capability_tags":["cf-node","deployment","verification"],"commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"worker_summary":null,"worker_status":"pending","foreman_note":"PREMISE DISPROVED 2026-11-05T13:02Z by live probe, minutes after this row was filed on the audit finding. Run from /home/kara/code-factory: bash scripts/verify-node.sh --agent cf-node --server bunker-las-03 --strict-freshness reports checkout_freshness PASS with branch=main head=cf50c6e19896 origin_main=cf50c6e19896 ancestor=true behind=0, so the node is NOT 2 commits behind - it is on origin/main. The script does not FAIL either: it exits 3 with VERIFY: UNVERIFIED, which is by design (nothing broken, nothing proven) because this host has no transport to the node gateway at 192.168.123.66:10800; that residual is already tracked by CF-224, so this row does not duplicate it. What closed the drift: CF-244 landed the freshness check at 8db72b3 and the sibling lane closed it at 2026-11-05T12:57:46Z (commit cf50c6e), and the node is now on that head. Why it is deferred rather than completed: no evidence run backs it and the premise is gone. Reopen only if a node reports behind > 0 or an ancestor=false in checkout_freshness.","deferred":true}
 {"id":"CF-249","title":"A real foreman directive makes the node harness run 39 minutes and return 36 bytes, and nothing records what it was doing","status":"in_progress","priority":"P1","complexity":3,"reasoning":null,"acceptance_criteria":"1. A directive that takes longer than the poll interval produces a progress record an operator can read WHILE it runs: at minimum the last tool call and its elapsed time, written at a fixed cadence.\n2. When such a run is killed, the record says what it was doing at the moment of the kill, so the failure is attributable rather than 'it hung'.\n3. The node session store shows the conversation so far on a killed run: today a 39-minute run leaves exactly one message (the user prompt) and no assistant or tool rows.\n4. A test reproduces the hang with a directive of comparable size and asserts that progress was recorded before the deadline, so this cannot regress silently.","probe":null,"created_at":"2026-11-05T13:05:08Z","updated_at":"2026-11-05T13:15:31Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"71cf4e64109923824af218d6d68b5607f57727f6bd73c97e2539ddd989baff9f"},"capability_tags":[],"commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"worker_summary":null,"worker_status":"pending","foreman_note":"Evidence, 2026-11-04. The durable path started job-1793881486-969735cc on cf-node with the real 4,046-byte foreman directive at 07:24:56 and killed it at 08:03:58: rc=124 after 2342s (39 minutes). Its out.log is 36 bytes and contains only 'session_id: 20261105_042456_716a72'. The node's state.db has exactly ONE message for that session — the user prompt — so no assistant or tool activity was persisted for the whole run. The same node answers 'ALIVE-CHECK' in seconds for a short prompt (session 20261105_050420_fe00cc), and the 400s boundary job returned BOUNDARY-CROSSED, so the harness and the job model both work; it is this class of directive that hangs. Nothing in the run can be attributed beyond 'it hung', which is why the row asks for progress records rather than more retries.\n\nImplemented and observed 2026-11-04. run.sh starts a heartbeat that appends '<UTC time> hp=<pid> <elapsed> <cmdline>' to progress.log every 20s; the dispatcher polls that line and logs it when it changes. Live example from job job-1793884459-472317b8: '13:14:48 hp=1292325 00:20 timeout 150 /home/bunker-cf-node/.local/bin/hermes chat -q Write a 600 word essay about tundra. -Q' then '00:40' on the next line, finishing rc=0 at 55s. Three defects were found and fixed while making it true: GNU timeout runs the command in its own process group (so a run.sh pgid scan reports idle for a live harness), ps --no-headers is unsupported in the node image, and ps output contains non-UTF8 bytes that crashed subprocess text=True at three call sites (now errors=replace). AC1 is met and observed; AC2 (what it was doing at the kill) follows from the same record but has not yet been captured on a killed real run; AC3 (session store shows only the user message on a killed run) is still true and unfixed."}
 {"id": "CF-250", "title": "P2 — nothing on the control host reports seed drift: verify-node.sh has no seed leg, so a node whose prompts or skills were edited by hand still reports green", "status": "pending", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 2, "reasoning": "Measured 2026-11-05 by the diag-node-1 tick while closing CF-220. The seed contract is real and it can go red on the node: `python3 $HOME/node_seed.py check --record $HOME/.hermes/seed-applied.json --home $HOME` printed `FAIL seed_check — prompts/foreman.md drifted (75da16fb93fd != 82c020b6f316)` and exit 1 after one line was appended to a seeded prompt, and `PASS seed_check — 13 files present and matching` after the file was restored (docs/audits/code-factory-cf220-2026-11-05.md). Nothing on the control host invokes it. `scripts/verify-node.sh` folds exactly one node-tree probe into VERIFY: — checkout_freshness, added by CF-244 — and grep for `seed` in verify-node.sh returns nothing; `scripts/project-node.sh` runs `node_seed.py build|apply` at provision time only. So the operator-visible verdict over a live node cannot see a hand-edited prompt or skill, and after provisioning deletes $HOME/node_seed.py and $HOME/seed.tar* the only copy of the checker on the node is gone until something stages it again. This is the same class CF-244 closed for the checkout: the instrument exists, the control-host leg does not.", "acceptance_criteria": "1. `scripts/verify-node.sh --agent <id> --server <host>` prints a `seed_drift` row: PASS naming the file count when the node's seeded tree matches its record, FAIL naming each drifted or absent path and the expected vs measured digest prefix when it does not. The row is produced by one `bunker exec` round trip, in the idiom of the CF-244 freshness leg (stage node_seed.py to a temp path, run `check`, remove it).\n2. A node with no `$HOME/.hermes/seed-applied.json` reports WARN naming the absent record and `--strict-seed` turns that into FAIL; exit-code semantics stay distinguishable from the freshness leg's (a drifted seed alone makes `VERIFY: FAIL`).\n3. `tests/selftest.sh` gains a section proving both directions offline, against a fixture node directory and a fixture bunker shim (no network): green arm PASS with the file count, red arm FAIL naming the drifted path, absent-record arm WARN then FAIL under `--strict-seed`. Each arm must be able to go the other way, per AGENTS.md rule 2.\n4. `specs/NODE.md` records the new leg in the same table cell that documents checkout_freshness, and `docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md` counts are updated to the measured selftest section count.\n5. `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints SELFTEST: PASS at the fixing commit, and the row's closeout quotes the live command and output for one real node (cf-node on bunker-las-03), green and, with a single appended line, red.", "created_at": "2026-11-05T13:15:08Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-05T13:15:08Z"}
+{"id": "CF-251", "title": "cf-node is absent from the fleet repo-scope manifest, so every job it runs is refused a GitHub token", "status": "pending", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 2, "reasoning": null, "acceptance_criteria": "1) fleet-repo-scope.json carries an entry for cf-node scoped to coding-hermes/code-factory only. 2) The dispatcher's job-boundary test stops printing 'no scoped token for cf-node' and proves a scoped token is issued. 3) A token issued for cf-node cannot reach any repo outside its declared scope - negative case asserted, not asserted in prose. 4) The manifest is validated at dispatch time so a missing agent is a named refusal, not a silent unauthenticated job.", "created_at": "2026-11-05T13:42:27Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-05T13:42:27Z", "detail": {"fingerprint": "53ebae6e07a65534f1d764e70a6d79548a0048c9619ab6e479f79accf6a5f784"}}
